    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.bufremove\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nVim provides a native `:confirm` command for operations that require confirmation, such as when closing unsaved buffers. It would be nice if `mini.bufremove` can use this to allow the user to confirm unsaved changes.",
